  "conclusion": "The new persistence diagnostics show that cold-arrival survival is real but usually short-lived or missed by the diagnostic cadence. run01 had one origin-k=6 cluster-sector change; it reached cold already reverted, stayed in cold for 4 transport samples, missed the stride-4 sector diagnostic, and departed reverted. run02 had no cluster-stage sector changes. run03 had 131 cluster-stage sector changes and 74 cold arrivals; 20 were survived at first cold contact, 26 reverted, and 28 landed in another signature. Only 2 arrivals were actually seen by the next sector diagnostic as survived while 68 missed the diagnostic cadence; at cold departure the 74 arrivals were split into 20 survived, 26 reverted, and 28 other. Thus survived-at-arrival is not a pure diagnostic artifact, but most arrivals are too transient for the sector diagnostic and even survived arrivals do not produce stable cold-slot sector flips."
}
